{"term":"semen","lang":"es","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"fluids_states","subcategory":"semen","concept":"semen","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"clinical","crude":20,"technical":95,"recognition_pct_current":90,"recognition_pct_peak":90,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Semen; the clinical Spanish term for the seminal fluid ejaculated from the penis at orgasm, composed of spermatozoa and secretions from the prostate and seminal vesicles.","english_term":"semen","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Identical in form and meaning to the English clinical term; a direct Latin borrowing. Recognized without stigma across all Spanish-speaking regions and registers."}
{"term":"esperma","lang":"es","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"fluids_states","subcategory":"semen","concept":"semen","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":25,"technical":65,"recognition_pct_current":85,"recognition_pct_peak":85,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Sperm or semen; colloquially used for the entire seminal ejaculate rather than strictly the gamete cells, occupying a middle ground between clinical and everyday registers.","english_term":"sperm / semen","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Technically refers to sperm cells (see espermatozoides) but in common usage often means the whole ejaculate interchangeably with 'semen.' Less crude than slang alternatives such as 'leche' or 'lefa.'"}
