{"term":"leche","lang":"es","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"fluids_states","subcategory":"semen","concept":"semen","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":80,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":82,"recognition_pct_peak":82,"peak_year":null,"regional":"ES","definition":"Iberian crude slang for semen; literally 'milk,' one of the most versatile and prevalent vulgar terms in Peninsular Spanish, functioning also as a general expletive and intensifier.","english_term":"cum / jizz","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Primarily Iberian Spanish. In most of Latin America 'leche' retains only its dairy meaning and the semen sense reads as bizarre. In Spain it operates across multiple vulgar registers beyond the semen sense ('¡Me cago en la leche!', 'qué mala leche')."}
{"term":"lefa","lang":"es","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"fluids_states","subcategory":"semen","concept":"semen","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":92,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":58,"recognition_pct_peak":62,"peak_year":null,"regional":"ES","definition":"Highly vulgar Iberian slang for semen or ejaculate; among the crudest and most explicit terms for seminal fluid in Peninsular Spanish, with essentially no non-vulgar contexts of use.","english_term":"jizz / spunk / cum","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Virtually unknown in Latin America. Etymology is debated. Carries a stronger transgressive charge than 'leche' and appears almost exclusively in pornographic, crudely humorous, or shock-value contexts."}
{"term":"corrida","lang":"es","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"fluids_states","subcategory":"ejaculation","concept":"ejaculation","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":75,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":73,"recognition_pct_peak":73,"peak_year":null,"regional":"ES","definition":"Iberian slang for an ejaculation, orgasm, or cumshot; derived from the reflexive verb 'correrse' (to come/orgasm); also the standard Spanish word for a bullfight.","english_term":"cumshot / orgasm / come","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"The dual meaning (bullfight vs. ejaculation) generates bawdy wordplay in Spain. In Latin America 'corrida' means a run or bullfight with no ejaculation sense; the productive base verb 'correrse' is pan-Hispanic but the nominalized sexual 'corrida' is Iberian-specific."}
